@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:architecture] sparkle-translates-through-macros
Sparkle components MUST translate with the macros (`@lingui/react/macro`, `@lingui/core/macro`).
They MUST NOT import `useLingui`, `Trans`, `I18nProvider` or `i18n` from `@lingui/react` or
`@lingui/core`: those would show front's translations, which don't include sparkle's text.
`src/lib/i18n/` is the exception, since it uses them to set up sparkle's own translations.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:product] sparkle-lingui-files-fully-translated
A file under `src/` (excluding `src/stories/`) that uses a Lingui macro MUST translate every
user-visible string it renders by default, including `aria-label`, `placeholder`, `title` and
tooltip text. A text prop the consumer may override MUST be rendered as given when defined, and fall
back to the translated default only when `undefined` (``{label ?? t`Load more`}``), not through a
hardcoded English default value.

@cc [owner:ykmsd,label:product] sparkle-formats-through-format-module
Code under `src/` (excluding `src/stories/`, `src/lib/i18n/` and the deprecated
`src/components/Document/`) MUST format user-visible numbers, dates and relative times with the
functions of `src/lib/i18n/format.ts` (adding the missing one there), passing the locale of
`useFormatLocale` unless the consumer provided one. It MUST NOT call `Intl` formatters or
`toLocaleString`, `toLocaleDateString` and `toLocaleTimeString` directly: those ignore the format
locale of `SparkleI18nProvider` (e.g. `en-GB`, which renders the `en-US` catalog).
